00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:16.717
The grip: right hand in a continental grip at the bottom of the handle, left hand in a forehand grip above it.

00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:19.380
Keep both hands close together, with no gap.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.743
Ready position: feet one and a half shoulder widths apart, knees slightly bent, weight low,

00:00:24.743 --> 00:00:27.080
arms naturally bent in front of your body.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:34.140
Loading phase: turn your body to take the racket back. Beginners should get into the habit of not pulling it back with the hands.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.600
Hold the racket crosswise to feel how the turn of the body moves it.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:46.260
How far to turn: left shoulder toward the ball, the racket turns with the body to six o'clock.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000 line:10%
